p to 3 attempts in total. I checked it against a real local HTTP server and every case behaved as expected.\n\n**How it works:**\n- `urlopen` raises an `HTTPError` on a 503. The client catches it, waits, and tries again.\n- The wait doubles each time: 0.5s after the first failure, 1s after the second.\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is raised to the caller as before.\n- Any other HTTP error, or a network failure, is raised straight away with no retry.\n- Two new constructor settings: `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5` (the first wait, in seconds). Existing calls work unchanged.\n\n**Test results** (with the first wait shortened to 0.05s):\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | returns the JSON | 3 |\n| 503, 503, 503 | raises `HTTPError 503` | 3 |\n| 500 | raises `HTTPError 500` | 1 |\n| 200 | returns the JSON | 1 |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so this check was a one-off script and nothing new is saved in the repo.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 70012, "requests_cache_write": 142935, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7647134000000001, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1799, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 0, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:36:22.169171+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 24.862, "t_checker_s": 2.436, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1813, "tokens_cache_read