03. It makes at most 3 attempts and waits longer between each one.\n\n- **Retries:** only a 503 response is retried. Any other HTTP error, such as a 500, is raised straight away. If all 3 attempts get a 503, it raises that last 503 error.\n- **Backoff:** the wait doubles each time. With the default `backoff=0.5` it waits 0.5s, then 1s. There's no wait after the last attempt.\n- **Settings:** I added two constructor arguments, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5`. With the defaults, existing callers get the new retry behaviour without changing anything.\n- **Not retried:** timeouts and connection errors still fail on the first attempt, because you asked for 503 only. The `Retry-After` header is ignored.\n\nI checked it against a real local HTTP server with `backoff=0.05`:\n\n| Server responses | Result | Time |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | returns the data | 0.16s |\n| 503, 503, 503 | raises the 503 error | 0.15s |\n| 500 | raises at once, no retry | 0.00s |\n| 200 | returns the data | 0.00s |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add a test file.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 105456, "requests_cache_write": 73396, "requests_cost_usd": 0.42345920000000004, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1767, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 2, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:36:23.942445+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 22.754, "t_checker_s": 2.482, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "tok