akes at most 3 attempts in total, waiting longer between each one.\n\n- **What retries:** only HTTP 503. Any other HTTP error, such as a 500, is raised straight away without retrying.\n- **Wait times:** the client waits `backoff` seconds after the first failure, then twice that after the second. The default `backoff` is 0.5s, so the waits are 0.5s and 1s. You can pass a different value when creating the client: `WeatherClient(..., backoff=...)`.\n- **After 3 failures:** if all three attempts get a 503, the last 503 error is raised to the caller.\n- I added `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3` as a class attribute, so the attempt count is set in one place.\n\nI tested it in a one-off script against a real local HTTP server. I didn't add any test files to the repo.\n\n| Server responses | Requests made | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | 3 | returns the data |\n| 503, 503, 503 | 3 | raises the 503 error |\n| 500 | 1 | raises the 500 error, no retry |\n| 200 | 1 | returns the data |", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 69818, "requests_cache_write": 143597, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7669045999999999, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1745, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial5", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 8, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:36:49.261446+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 23.224, "t_checker_s": 2.441, "t_env_setup_s": 0.149, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1759, "tokens_cache_read": 69818,